## SECTION 2: WHAT'S INCLUDED

**Section headline:** What Foundation includes

**Loki AI Agent — Helpdesk Support**
Loki — Klaravex's AI agent — is your first line of support, available 24/7. Common device issues, account problems, and IT questions handled instantly. When Loki can't resolve it, a senior engineer steps in with defined response SLAs.

**M365 / Azure Management and User Support**
User provisioning and deprovisioning, license management, Exchange Online administration, Teams setup and troubleshooting, SharePoint and OneDrive configuration. Ongoing management, not just break-fix.

**Google Workspace Management and User Support**
User administration, group management, Gmail and Drive configuration, Workspace app setup and troubleshooting — where applicable.

**AWS Operational Support**
Basic IAM management, billing alert configuration, and resource management. Scoped per engagement — not full AWS security management (that's Assurance or Directive).

**Ubiquiti UniFi Network and Firewall Management**
Firewall rule management, VLAN configuration, firmware updates, and network monitoring for UniFi environments — where applicable.

**Endpoint Management**
Microsoft Intune or equivalent MDM — device enrollment, policy deployment, and compliance reporting.

**Security Configuration Baseline**
MFA enforcement, conditional access baselines, and security hygiene configuration. This is baseline security — not ongoing threat monitoring or vulnerability management (that's Assurance or Directive).

**Monthly Operations Report**
A concise monthly report covering support activity, open items, and operational health across your managed platforms.

---

## SECTION 3: PLATFORM COVERAGE CALLOUT
*(Callout box)*

Foundation covers the platforms you run. M365/Azure, Google Workspace, and AWS are all supported — scope is defined per engagement.

---

## SECTION 4: IMPORTANT — KNOW WHAT FOUNDATION IS
*(Visible positioning note — per PRD requirement)*

Foundation is our operational baseline — not our security advisory offering.

If your organization has regulatory requirements, an upcoming audit, a breach to recover from, or a readiness program to build, you likely need Assurance or Directive. Foundation is the right fit for growing businesses that need reliable, well-managed IT operations — not a compliance program.

Foundation clients can upgrade to Assurance or Directive at any time.

---

## SECTION 5: WHEN TO CONSIDER UPGRADING
*(Upgrade path)*

**Section headline:** When Foundation clients move up

- You receive a security questionnaire from a customer or partner that requires formal documentation
- Your industry has regulatory requirements (HIPAA, SOC 2, NIS2, GDPR) that need an advisory program
- You've had a security incident or near-miss and need proactive monitoring
- Your team has grown past 20–25 users and security hygiene alone isn't enough
- A new enterprise customer requires proof of your security posture as a condition of doing business

---

## SECTION 6: SCOPE DISCLAIMER
*(Mandatory callout box)*

Service scope, regulatory applicability, and readiness claims are defined per engagement in a written Statement of Work. Klaravex does not issue compliance certifications or attestations. Readiness advisory and preparation services are not a substitute for an independent audit or certification body assessment.

